    <!-- Root Explanations -->
    <string name="root_check_content">
        Your phone is rooted. Awesome!
        We will ask for the root permission next.
        If you choose to deny it, the app will still work, but there will be a prompt before each app is uninstalled.
        \nUnfortunately, this is a limitation of the Android system.
    </string>
    <string name="no_root_check_content">
        Your phone is not rooted.
        The app will still work, but there will be a prompt before each app is uninstalled.
        Unfortunately, this is a limitation of the Android system.
        However, this process will still be faster than uninstalling them from the settings menu.
    </string>
    <string name="root_system_app">
        Uninstalling certain system apps can brick the device/render it unusable in some cases.
        Select ONLY if you are absolutely sure.
    </string>
    <string name="no_root_system_app">
        System apps can only be restored to the original installed version.
        They cannot be uninstalled completely without root permissions.
    </string>
    <string name="root_grant_ask">
        We will ask for root permissions now.
        If your phone is not rooted, or you don\'t want to use root, you can deny it.
    </string>
    <string name="system_app_reboot">
        You have uninstalled one or more system apps.
        To remove them from the launcher and app drawer, you need to reboot the phone.
    </string>

    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_text">
        A batch uninstaller based on Batch Uninstaller by Sarbajit Saha.
        Works best if phone is rooted. Debloat information is from MuntashirAkon’s Android Debloat List (AGPL-3.0).
        \n\nThis app is open-source and can be found on GitHub!
    </string>
